    "title": "The 2026 Oscars winners list: 'One Battle After Another,' Sinners,' all the night’s wins!",
    "text": "It’s been a long awards season, but we’re finally here at the finish line: the 2026 Oscars!This image released by Warner Bros. Pictures shows Leonardo DiCaprio in a scene from \"One Battle After Another.\" (Warner Bros. Pictures via AP)“Sinners” broke records with its 16 nominations, but it couldn't quite beat \"One Battle After Another, which took home six of its 13 nominations, including Best Picture, Best Director, Best Editing, Best Adapted Screenplay, Best Supporting Actor, and Best Casting. \"Sinners\" did take home four of it's 16 nominations, including Best Original Screenplay, Best Score, Best Cinematography, and Best Actor.We got the first ever award for Best Casting, which went to \"One Battle After Another.\"And we had one of the biggest surprises of the night in the Best Live Action Short with a tie between the films \"The Singers\" and \"Two People Exchanging Saliva.\" There have only been six ties in Oscar history, the most famous being between Barbra Streisand and Katherine Hepburn in 1969 for Best Actress. Check out the full list of winners below!Best Picture“One Battle After Another”This image released by Warner Bros. Pictures shows Leonardo DiCaprio in a scene from \"One Battle After Another.\" (Warner Bros. Pictures via AP)Best DirectorPaul Thomas Anderson, “One Battle After Another”LEONARDO DI CAPRIO as Bob Ferguson in “One Battle After Another.” A Warner Bros. Pictures Release.Best ActorMichael B. Jordan, “Sinners”Michael B. Jordan was nominated for Best Actor for \"Sinners.\" (Courtesy Warner Bros. Pictures)Best ActressJessie Buckley, “Hamnet”4238_D045_00238_RJessie Buckley stars as Agnes and Joe Alwyn as Bartholomew in director Chloé Zhao’s HAMNET, a Focus Features release.Credit: Agata Grzybowska / © 2025 FOCUS FEATURES LLCBest Supporting ActorSean Penn, “One Battle After Another”(L-r) TEYANA TAYLOR as Perfidia and SEAN PENN as Col. Steven J. Lockjaw in “One Battle After Another.” A Warner Bros. Pictures Release.Best Supporting ActressAmy Madigan, “Weapons”Oscar-nominee Amy Madigan as Aunt Gladys in \"Weapons.\" (Courtesy: Warner Bros.)Best Original Screenplay“Sinners”MICHAEL B. JORDAN as Smoke and as Stack, in Warner Bros. Pictures’ “SINNERS,” a Warner Bros. Pictures release.Best Adapted Screenplay“One Battle After Another”TEYANA TAYLOR as Perfidia in “One Battle After Another.” A Warner Bros. Pictures Release.Best Casting“One Battle After Another”CHASE INFINITI as Willa Ferguson in “One Battle After Another.” A Warner Bros. Pictures Release.Best Animated Feature“KPop Demon Hunters”KPOP DEMON HUNTERS - When they aren't selling out stadiums, Kpop superstars Rumi, Mira and Zoey use their secret identities as badass demon hunters to protect their fans from an ever-present supernatural threat. Together, they must face their biggest enemy yet – an irresistible rival boy band of demons in disguise. ©2025 NetflixBest Production Design“Frankenstein”FRANKENSTEIN. (L to R) Jacob Elordi as the Creature and Oscar Isaac as Victor Frankenstein n Frankenstein. Cr. Ken Woroner/Netflix © 2025.Best Cinematography“Sinners”WUNMI MOSAKU as Annie and MICHAEL B. JORDAN as Stack in Warner Bros. Pictures’ “SINNERS,” a Warner Bros. Pictures release. (Courtesy of Warner Bros. Pictures)Best Costume Design“Frankenstein”Jacob Elordi as \"The Creature\" in Guillermo del Toro's \"Frankenstein.\" (Courtesy of Netflix)Best Film Editing“One Battle After Another”Warner Bros unveils trailer for One Battle After Another with scenes shot in El Paso featuring Leonardio DiCaprio (credit: Warner Bros)Best Makeup and Hairstyling“Frankenstein”FRANKENSTEIN. Jacob Elordi as The Creature in Frankenstein. Cr. Ken Woroner/Netflix © 2025.Best Sound“F1”Brad Pitt in \"F1.\" (Photo by Scott Garfield. Courtesy Warner Bros Pictures / Apple Original Films)Best Visual Effects“Avatar: Fire and Ash”Varang (Oona Chaplin) in 20th Century Studios' AVATAR: FIRE AND ASH. Photo courtesy of 20th Century Studios. © 2025 20th Century Studios. All Rights Reserved.Best Original Score“Sinners”Warner Bros. Pictures’ “SINNERS,” a Warner Bros. Pictures release.Best Original Song“Golden” from “KPop Demon Hunters”KPOP DEMON HUNTERS - When they aren't selling out stadiums, Kpop superstars Rumi, Mira and Zoey use their secret identities as badass demon hunters to protect their fans from an ever-present supernatural threat. Together, they must face their biggest enemy yet – an irresistible rival boy band of demons in disguise. ©2025 NetflixBest Documentary Feature“Mr. Nobody Against Putin”Best International Feature“Sentimental Value”This image released by Neon shows Renate Reinsve, left, and Inga Ibsdotter Lilleaas in a scene from \"Sentimental Value.\" (Kasper Tuxen/Neon via AP)Best Animated Short“The Girl Who Cried Pearls”Best Documentary Short“All the Empty Rooms”Best Live Action Short(TIED) “The Singers” and “Two People Exchanging Saliva”",
